#!/usr/bin/env bash
# xcodebuild — a PATH SHIM for unattended sessions. Not a build tool: it inspects the argv, refuses the
# one form that takes over the owner's physical screen, and otherwise execs the real xcodebuild untouched.
#
# WHY A SHIM AND NOT (JUST) A HOOK. `.claude/hooks/no-host-gui.sh` matches the Bash tool's COMMAND STRING,
# so it only ever sees what the model typed. On 2026-07-30 a daemon session ran `./ArchiveNotes/test-smoke.sh`
# — a string containing no `xcodebuild` and no `-only-testing` — and the script's own
#     xcodebuild test -scheme ArchiveNotes -destination platform=macOS
# ran the scheme's UITest bundle on the host: ArchiveNotesUITests-Runner.app driving the real app, the
# "Automation Running" banner, minutes of the owner's screen. A wrapper script defeats a string matcher at
# any depth. This shim sits on the child's PATH instead, so it catches the exec itself no matter how many
# scripts deep it happens. (Both test-smoke.sh scripts call bare `xcodebuild`, which is what makes this
# work; a caller using an absolute Xcode path would bypass it, hence hook + shim + source guard, not one.)
#
# ACTIVE ONLY when ARCHIVE_UNATTENDED=1 — the owner's interactive sessions get the real tool, unchanged.
#
# THE RULE: a `test` action must name a bundle with `-only-testing:`. Without one, xcodebuild runs the
# scheme's whole test action, which for ArchiveReader/ArchiveNotes includes the *UITests bundle. Refused.
# Everything else — build, build-for-testing, archive, -showBuildSettings, clean, and any
# `-only-testing:<App>Tests` unit run (windowless since ArchiveCore ArchiveTestHost) — passes straight through.

REAL="${ARCHIVE_REAL_XCODEBUILD:-/usr/bin/xcodebuild}"
[ -x "$REAL" ] || REAL="$(/usr/bin/which -a xcodebuild 2>/dev/null | grep -v "ops/autonomous/bin" | head -1)"

if [ "${ARCHIVE_UNATTENDED:-0}" != "1" ]; then exec "$REAL" "$@"; fi

has_test_action=0 has_only_testing=0
for a in "$@"; do
  case "$a" in
    test|test-without-building) has_test_action=1 ;;
    -only-testing|-only-testing:*) has_only_testing=1 ;;
  esac
done

if [ "$has_test_action" = 1 ] && [ "$has_only_testing" = 0 ]; then
  cat >&2 <<'EOF'
BLOCKED by ops/autonomous/bin/xcodebuild (host-GUI shim, active because ARCHIVE_UNATTENDED=1)

A bare `xcodebuild test` runs the scheme's ENTIRE test action. For ArchiveReader and ArchiveNotes that
includes the UITest bundle, which drives the real app on the owner's physical display for minutes and
raises the macOS "Automation Running" banner. That is not allowed in an unattended session.

Do this instead:
  * unit tests  ->  xcodebuild test -only-testing:<App>Tests ...
                    (app-hosted, but windowless since ArchiveCore `ArchiveTestHost`)
  * UITests     ->  ops/gui/vm-gui-runner.sh <reader|notes> xcuitest
                    (the same tests, off-screen in the headless Tart VM)

If you got here through a wrapper script (e.g. `./ArchiveNotes/test-smoke.sh`), that script has an
unattended mode that runs only the unit bundle — it should have been used. Do not work around this shim;
if a check genuinely cannot run off-screen, leave it for the owner in the Morning Review list.
EOF
  exit 74
fi

exec "$REAL" "$@"
